		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Physics Shader - Just a thought]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=30186#p30186"><![CDATA[
I think that all GPU physics can only be used for visual effects. Imagine you could run all physics in one millisecond (which you cant). It will take three frames until you get the result due to latency. Shared memory might help with this, but you would have to divide the rendering into chunks such that you can interleave physics and graphics. I doubt this will happen. For me all this GPU physics is just a marketing hype by the GPU vendors. <br><br>There is really only one important question to answer in this context. Will we get better games with GPU physics? My answer is no. That is why you are not seeing anything in this context.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Wed Mar 06, 2013 4:19 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
